## Fixed protocol (per researcher)
Headline contrast `Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50` (9_1..9_3) vs `DMSO` (3_1..3_3), 3v3;
DE filter baseMean>10 & \|log2FC\|>0.5 & **nominal** Wald p<0.05 (padj reported); pooled up+down;
universe = expressed + real symbol (15,206 genes / 15,199 symbols); multi-ENSG->same symbol resolved
by highest baseMean; enrichment = hypergeometric ORA + BH (gseapy.enrichr-equivalent, labelled as such).

## Two implementation decisions forced by the environment (both evidence-backed)
1. **No R/DESeq2/pydeseq2** -> NB2 GLM implemented in numpy/scipy with library-size **offsets**
   (`mu_ij = s_j * q_group`). Forgetting the offsets inflates dispersion ~100x (0.29 vs 0.014) and
   kills the test; validated against `statsmodels` NB GLM (r = 0.988 on Wald z, 0.990 on -log10 p).
2. **Dispersion trend from the MoM mean, not the median.** 40 random 3v3 relabellings of the same
   6 libraries: median-based trend -> 0.31 of all genes "p<0.05" (badly anti-conservative);
   mean-based trend -> 0.038 (target 0.05). Null DE calls 289 (median) / 359 (q95) vs 1,070 observed,
   so the real signal is far above the permutation floor. Gene-wise MAP shrinkage was not used
   (n=3 per group); this is edgeR-style trended dispersion, a deliberate, documented deviation from
   DESeq2's MAP estimator.

## Status
DE analysis: **executed**. Enrichment: **NOT RUN** — gseapy absent, zero network egress (DNS fails and
raw TCP to public IPs returns `ENETUNREACH`), no Reactome/GMT content anywhere on the filesystem.
No substitute/hand-built gene-set library was used. To finish in one command once the library exists:
`REACTOME_GMT=/path/to/Reactome_2022.symbols.gmt python3 analysis/de_enrichment_pipeline.py`

## Status of the marker panels (read this before quoting anything)
`results/de_signature_panels_DIAGNOSTIC.csv` and the panel lines in the handoff use
**gene lists I wrote by hand**. They are not a Reactome_2022 collection and they are not an
enrichment result; they are a hypothesis generated by reading the DE table. The requested
gseapy/Reactome_2022 ORA was **not executed**. Note also that AHRR and CYP1A1 do *not* pass the
DE filter against `CBD_IC50` alone (log2FC +0.38 / +0.24), so the AhR/xenobiotic arm is
attributable to CBD rather than to the combination — see
`results/axis_robustness_across_controls.csv`.
